-- title:
--   Every functional on the Hecke span is T↦ a₁(Tf)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a non-zero natural number and let $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ denote the space of cusp forms of weight $2$ for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_0(N)$. Let $\varphi$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-linear functional on the whole endomorphism algebra $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$. The assertion is that there exists a cusp form $f \in S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ such that for every operator $T$ lying in the $\mathbb{C}$-linear span of [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) one has $\varphi(T) = a_1(Tf)$, where $a_1(g)$ is the coefficient of index $1$ in the $q$-expansion of $g$ with respect to the period $1$, i.e. [`ModularFormClass.qCoeff (T f) 1`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L19). Here [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin 2 hℓ hℓN` for all primes $\ell$ not dividing $N$ together with the operators `heckeULin 2 hqN` for all primes $q$ dividing $N$, the excluded set of primes being empty; $\varphi$ is unconstrained off this span, so the conclusion only pins down $\varphi$ on the span.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the duality between the weight-two Hecke algebra at level $N$ and $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ under the pairing $(T,f)\mapsto a_1(Tf)$: every functional on the complex Hecke span is realised by a cusp form. It is used in the construction of an integral structure on $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ ([`CuspForm.hasIntegralStructure_two`](thm.html#CuspForm.hasIntegralStructure_two)).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_form_of_functional_span_heckeAlgebra.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_FLTPrelim_Modularity

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.exists_form_of_functional_span_heckeAlgebra (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (φ : Module.End ℂ (CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2) →ₗ[ℂ] ℂ) :
    ∃ f : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2,
      ∀ T ∈ Submodule.span ℂ (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (∅ : Set ℕ) : Set (Module.End ℂ (CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2))), φ T = ModularFormClass.qCoeff (T f) 1 := by sorry
